@retrieval-arm-switch @memory-ablation
Feature: Fleet-Memory Retrieval Arm Switch and Retrieval Logging
  As a memory-ablation operator
  I want an in-client retrieval arm switch and per-item retrieval logging
  So that ablation rollouts can toggle memory retrieval without diverging any other code path and every retrieval call is auditable

  Background:
    Given a clean process environment with no retrieval arm selected

  # ============================================================================
  # GROUP A: Key Examples
  # ============================================================================

  # Why: Core off-arm gate — retrieval is suppressed inside the client so the
  # loader, turn-continuation and template-pattern chain stays intact
  @task:TASK-ABL1-004
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Off arm suppresses retrieval inside the client without touching the loader chain
    Given the retrieval arm is set to "off"
    And the fleet-memory backend is enabled
    When an AutoBuild context search is performed
    Then the search should return no results
    And the memory store should not be queried
    And no retrieval-log entry should be written
    And the AutoBuild context loader should still be constructed

  # Why: Core fixture-arm path — corpus swap plus a per-item audit trail
  @task:TASK-ABL1-004
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Fixture arm resolves the fixture corpus and logs per-item identity
    Given the retrieval arm is set to "fixture:v1"
    And the fixture DSN for "v1" is provided via the environment
    And the fleet-memory backend is enabled
    When an AutoBuild context search returns stored items
    Then the store connection should use the fixture DSN instead of the live DSN
    And a retrieval-log entry should record one item per result with its natural key and score
    And the logged item ids should be store natural keys rather than synthetic identifiers

  # Why: The unset arm must remain byte-identical to today's behaviour
  @task:TASK-ABL1-002
  @key-example
  Scenario: Unset arm preserves current retrieval behaviour
    Given no retrieval arm is selected
    When the fleet-memory configuration is loaded from the environment
    Then the retrieval arm should be unset
    And the store DSN should be the live configured DSN
    And an AutoBuild context search should query the store as it does today

  # Why: The ablation's validity rests on zero code-path divergence between arms
  @task:TASK-ABL1-004
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Context loading reports the same retrieval status across arms
    Given two AutoBuild context loads that differ only in the retrieval arm being "off" versus "fixture:v1"
    When Player context is loaded for the same task in each arm
    Then both arms should report context status "retrieved"
    And the turn-continuation path should be exercised identically in both arms
    And the template-pattern path should be exercised identically in both arms

  # ============================================================================
  # GROUP B: Boundary Conditions
  # ============================================================================

  # Why: Blank value boundary — an empty string must not accidentally select an arm
  @task:TASK-ABL1-002
  @boundary
  Scenario: A blank retrieval arm value behaves as unset
    Given the retrieval arm environment variable is set to an empty string
    When the fleet-memory configuration is loaded from the environment
    Then the retrieval arm should be unset

  # Why: Zero-result boundary — the run guardrail must distinguish "retrieval attempted, nothing found" from "no retrieval"
  @task:TASK-ABL1-003
  @boundary
  Scenario: A fixture-arm search with no matching items still writes a retrieval-log entry
    Given the fixture arm is active with a resolvable fixture DSN
    When an AutoBuild context search matches no stored items
    Then a retrieval-log entry should be written with an empty items list
    And the search should return no results

  # Why: Just-outside boundary of the fixture form — an id-less fixture selector is invalid
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Set-but-invalid arm values fail closed to off-arm behaviour
  @task:TASK-ABL1-002
  @boundary @negative
  Scenario: A fixture selector without an id fails closed
    Given the retrieval arm is set to "fixture:"
    When the fleet-memory configuration is loaded from the environment
    Then a configuration warning should be recorded
    And retrieval should behave as the off arm

